---
import WikiPage from '../components/WikiPage.astro';
import FAQ from '../components/FAQ.astro';
import { siteImages } from '../data/images';
const cards = [
  { title: 'Tables', description: 'Browse table families, selected Cash prices, and resale examples.', href: '/furniture/tables/', icon: 'T' },
  { title: 'Chairs', description: 'Compare chair families for upgrading the dining area.', href: '/furniture/chairs/', icon: 'C' },
  { title: 'Decorations', description: 'Explore Tiles, counters, Table Tops, Dishwasher, and Choopy features.', href: '/decorations/', icon: 'D' },
  { title: 'Plank Table', description: 'Review the Plank Table purchase and resale values.', href: '/furniture/plank-table/', icon: 'P' },
  { title: 'Wood Table', description: 'Review the Wood Table purchase and resale values.', href: '/furniture/wood-table/', icon: 'W' },
  { title: 'Red Wooden Table', description: 'Check the Red Wooden Table purchase price and progression details.', href: '/furniture/red-wooden-table/', icon: 'R' },
];

const faqItems = [
  { question: 'What furniture should I upgrade first?', answer: 'Start with the part of the dining area that is limiting service, then compare the current shop price with the Cash available for ingredients and equipment.' },
  { question: 'Can furniture be sold?', answer: 'Furniture can have a resale value. Check the amount shown by the game before confirming a sale.' },
  { question: 'Do all furniture items use the same resale percentage?', answer: 'Do not assume one percentage applies to every item. Review the value displayed for the selected furniture before selling it.' },
];
---
<WikiPage title="Furniture" description="Browse Karinderya table and chair families, prices, and upgrade notes." kicker="Dining room guide" intro="Compare furniture options for upgrading your restaurant dining area." cards={cards} note="Better tables and chairs can improve tip chance and reduce the chance that customers leave." sourceIds={['wiki-furniture']} relatedLinks={[{ label: 'Tables', href: '/furniture/tables/' }, { label: 'Chairs', href: '/furniture/chairs/' }, { label: 'Sell furniture guide', href: '/guides/how-to-sell-furniture/' }, { label: 'Beginner guide', href: '/guides/beginner-guide/' }]} heroImage={siteImages.furnitureHero} tableOfContents>
  <p>Furniture shapes the dining area and gives players another path for improving their restaurant. Available families include Plank, Wood, Red Wooden, Integrated, Elegant Wooden, Parsons, Slat-back, and Royal.</p>

  <h2 id="how-furniture-works">How Furniture Works</h2>
  <p>Tables and chairs are restaurant upgrades with different shop values and progression levels. Better furniture can improve tip chance and reduce the chance that customers leave, while selling older pieces can recover part of their value.</p>

  <h2 id="tables-and-chairs">Tables and Chairs</h2>
  <p>Use the <a href="/furniture/tables/">Tables database</a> to compare table families and selected prices. The <a href="/furniture/chairs/">Chairs page</a> lists the chair families available for the dining area.</p>

  <h2 id="upgrade-strategy">Upgrade Strategy</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Keep enough Cash available for ingredients before buying furniture.</li>
    <li>Upgrade in manageable steps instead of replacing the whole dining area at once.</li>
    <li>Check the current purchase and resale values before replacing an item.</li>
    <li>Balance dining-room upgrades with stove capacity and service needs.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="selling-furniture">Selling Furniture</h2>
  <p>Select the furniture you want to replace and review the resale value shown by the game before confirming. The <a href="/guides/how-to-sell-furniture/">selling guide</a> includes table examples and a short replacement checklist.</p>

  <FAQ items={faqItems} />
</WikiPage>
